WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.910
Two texts slide onto a
desk: a local blog post,

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.230
and a leaflet from a cycle group.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.780
Next to them, a blank speech card.

4
00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:11.280
Your job: write the speech.

5
00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:15.320
Lines of text lift off the pages
and drift towards the card,

6
00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:17.410
then hover at its edge.

7
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:21.080
So how much of what you've
read is allowed to cross over?

8
00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:25.680
In this mission, you'll find out
what directed writing actually marks.

9
00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:28.490
Copy as much as you can,
to prove you read it?

10
00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.420
Or ignore the texts and be original?

11
00:00:31.470 --> 00:00:35.660
And you'll hunt through the blog
post for one sweeping claim.

12
00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: work out
how much you can borrow.
